}

docs {
  # Recurring Ticket Reminder (Manual)

  Manually runs the daily recurring-ticket reminder job. By default this is a
  **preview**: it returns who would be notified and the exact message, and sends nothing.

  ## Access
  SuperUser only. Returns 403 for all other roles.

  ## Body
  | Field  | Type    | Default | Description |
  |--------|---------|---------|-------------|
  | `send` | boolean | `false` | `false` = preview only (nothing sent). `true` = actually send the push notifications. |

  ⚠️ `"send": true` sends real notifications to real users.

  ## Who is reminded
  The **requestor** (the person who raised the ticket) of every recurring ticket that the
  next auto-reopen run will reopen:

  - `isRecurring = true` and the ticket is closed (acknowledged as Resolved)
  - `nextRecurringDate` falls between the last reopen run and the next one (00:05 server time)
  - the requestor's account is active

  Approvers are not included. They still get the usual "📋 New Request" push when the
  ticket reopens. Tickets whose recurring schedule was stopped (`Stop Recurring`) are skipped.

  ## Timing
  - The reopen job runs daily at **00:05** (server time) and reopens due tickets.
  - The reminder goes out the day before, so each requestor gets **one** reminder per cycle.
  - The reminder covers exactly the tickets the next reopen run will pick up, so running this
    request several times on the same day returns the same list.

  ## Automatic schedule
  The same job runs automatically via cron every day at **10:00 AM IST**.

  ## Notification content
  - Title: "🔁 Recurring ticket #123 reopens tomorrow"
  - Body: "\"Monthly server backup check\" will reopen automatically (every 4 months) and the approval cycle will restart."
    (purpose cut to 70 characters; interval shown as weekly / every 2 weeks / monthly /
    every 4 months / every 6 months / yearly)
  - type / action: `recurring_reminder`
  - channel_id: `rts_notifications`
  - tag: `recurring-reminder-<ticketId>`
  - Sent to web push **and** the mobile app (FCM).

  ## What happens on tap
  `url` = `/?openRequest=<ticketId>` → the web dashboard opens that ticket's details.

  Mobile (FCM data): `type` / `action` = `recurring_reminder`, `request_id`,
  `deepLink` = `FRONTEND_URL + /?openRequest=<ticketId>`.

  ## Response
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "sent": false,
    "count": 1,
    "recipients": [
      {
        "id": 123,
        "empId": "GN-1042",
        "name": "Sudhakar G Hegde",
        "title": "🔁 Recurring ticket #123 reopens tomorrow"
      }
    ]
  }
  ```
  - `id` — ticket number that reopens tomorrow
  - `empId` / `name` — the requestor who is (or would be) notified

  ## Command-line dry run
  From `rts_backend`: `node -r dotenv/config src/utils/recurringCron.js`
}
